WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.817
A bank holds three loans to small businesses. Each one may

00:03.917 --> 00:09.423
default this year, independently, with probability twenty percent. The bank doesn't

00:09.523 --> 00:12.935
care exactly which loans default. It cares how many.

00:15.033 --> 00:19.014
Turning outcomes into numbers is what a random variable does. And

00:19.114 --> 00:22.404
despite the name, it is neither random nor a variable.

00:23.500 --> 00:27.743
The sample space lists which loans default: no defaults, the

00:27.843 --> 00:31.001
first only, and so on, eight outcomes in all.

00:31.100 --> 00:34.820
A random variable Y is a rule that sends each outcome to a

00:34.920 --> 00:39.892
number: here, the number of D's. Every outcome gets exactly one arrow. That's

00:39.992 --> 00:43.911
all it is: a function from the sample space to the real line.

00:44.011 --> 00:47.666
The randomness comes from the outcome, not from the rule.

00:48.750 --> 00:52.083
Each outcome carries a probability. No defaults at all:

00:52.183 --> 00:55.266
point eight cubed, about point five one. Any single

00:55.366 --> 00:58.263
default pattern: point one two eight. And so on.

00:58.350 --> 01:02.592
To get the probability that Y equals a particular value, follow the

01:02.692 --> 01:07.193
arrows backwards and add up the probability of every outcome that lands

01:07.293 --> 01:10.758
there. Three outcomes land on one, so P of Y equals one

01:10.858 --> 01:14.971
is three times point one two eight: about point three eight. That

01:15.071 --> 01:18.730
list of values and probabilities is the distribution of Y.

01:18.916 --> 01:22.022
And nothing stops us defining other functions on the same

01:22.122 --> 01:25.171
sample space, like the loss in manat, fifty thousand for

01:25.271 --> 01:28.377
each default. Same outcomes, a different random variable.

01:29.466 --> 01:34.556
Randomness also enters through how we collect data. An auditor must visit

01:34.656 --> 01:39.390
five of a bank's twenty branches. A simple random sample means every

01:39.490 --> 01:43.655
set of five branches is equally likely to be the one chosen.

01:43.750 --> 01:45.840
Draw such a sample a few times, and keep

01:45.940 --> 01:48.195
track of how often each branch gets picked.

01:49.350 --> 01:53.908
After two thousand samples, every branch has been chosen in about a

01:54.008 --> 01:59.331
quarter of them. That's no accident: under simple random sampling, each unit's

01:59.431 --> 02:03.295
chance of being included is n over N, five out of twenty.

02:03.395 --> 02:07.953
No branch is favoured, which is exactly what makes the sample fair.

02:09.050 --> 02:13.076
So: a random variable is a function that turns outcomes into

02:13.176 --> 02:18.097
numbers. Its distribution comes from following the arrows back and adding

02:18.197 --> 02:22.430
up probability. And a simple random sample gives every unit the

02:22.530 --> 02:25.250
same chance, n over N, of being included.
